                <pb facs="1138" n="1128" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/8–3044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-30T23:00:00+03:00">August 30, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 30—4:39 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3231. ReDeptel 2066, August 29, 3 p.m. I have noted that the Department has given
                    Stepanov final terms on all points under discussion in connection with Fourth
                    Protocol financial proposal. I am so informing Mikoyan in connection with a
                    letter I am addressing to him on related matters. The Department has been most
                    cooperative and patient with the Soviets in what must have been most
                    exasperating negotiations and I hope that as a matter of principle no further
                    concessions will be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
